  "backdrop_art": {
    "source": "TREX/textures/backdrop_trail.jpg",
    "tool": "Built-in ImageGen, editing the jungle clearing artwork",
    "final_prompt": "Revise this background plate for a colorful prehistoric dinosaur game. The current flat clearing looks bulldozed with repeated flat horizontal texture and symmetrical borders. Replace that floor and reframe from a fixed elevated hillside lookout looking diagonally DOWN over the nearby forest floor. Ground takes up the lower THREE QUARTERS of the picture; far bank and distant forest are in the upper quarter, no long straight horizon or straight horizontal treeline. A big, gently curving worn dinosaur trail widens into an organic open area where a large animal can turn around. Center is unobstructed walkable earth: painterly natural broad irregular patches of damp umber, warm ochre sand, rusty clay and soft slate silt, a few faint irregular tracks, varied scales, no tiling, no linear striations, no uniform gravel or repetitive pebbles, no geometric pattern. Create distinct asymmetric colorful EDGE vignettes: at lower left a low reddish weathered rock outcrop and copper-orange, red and golden prehistoric bromeliads with chartreuse moss; right margin an exposed twisting root, plum-magenta fern fronds, turquoise lichen on shale. Rich layered emerald and teal canopy, mist and a small subtle rainbow over the distant forest in upper strip. Soft daylight from above/front-left. Keep edge clusters low and confined to outermost edges, especially avoid crossing the open ground with flowers and rocks. Preserve a clear walkable path across middle 80% of width between 25% and 92% of image height. Environment only, no animals, no people, no dinosaur, text or UI. Visually rich, grounded and photographic, strong natural colours, landscape 16:10."
